# ⛔⛔ EVERY .env VARIANT, NOT JUST THE THREE THAT WERE LISTED — 2026-08-23, session 31.
# `.env`, `.env.bak` and `.env.*.bak` were ignored. `.env.backup.phaseG` — written during
# PHASE G and holding 8 lines of KEYS — matched NONE of them, sat untracked for two days,
# and a `git add -A` while landing a session's work would have committed live private keys
# and pushed them admin -> preview -> main. The pattern below covers any suffix a future
# session invents. `.env.example` is already TRACKED and an ignore rule cannot untrack it,
# but the negation is here so the intent is readable.
.env.*
!.env.example

